== 2026-09-01 - Patch Notes ==
These patch notes are from the Official EverQuest Legends discord, posted on September 1, 2026

=== [[Plane of Sky]] Changes ===
* Players can now receive bonus quest loot drops in the Plane of Sky for the classes in their current loadout. The drops will go into your Personal Loot pool and are affected by your loot filters such as auto-store and auto-destroy.
** These bonus drops extend to all enemies that drop items used in [[Plane of Sky]] [[Plane of Sky#Plane of Sky Class Quests|class quests]] except for the lettered "Wind Rune" items. That means main bosses, Efreeti, and even regular enemies that are needed for specific drops like many of the enemies on Islands 6 and 7.
** The bonus drops are not guaranteed but there are separate chances for all of the classes in your loadout - meaning that on occasion you can have three additional items added to your personal loot for a single kill!

=== Loadout Improvements ===
* You can now change your gender as part of configuring a loadout.
* Your currently selected face and eyes now save and can be stored as part of Loadouts.

=== General ===
* [[Levitation]] spells have had their descent rate adjusted to be consistent when slowly floating down.

=== Achievements ===
* [[Kerra|Kerran]] now count for the "Not a Kerran the World!" Achievement.
* Various Achievements are now marked optional that are not completable in the current expansion.
* The achievements relating to zones Freeport Sewers, Jaggedpine Forest, Caverns of Exile, and Nedaria's Landing are no longer active as they are inaccessible.
* The achievement Hunter of Toxxulia Forest is no longer active as it no longer has any valid targets.

=== AAs ===
* Full Potential will now autogrant at level 50. If you previously did not receive this AA, swap to any level 50 Loadout and zone.
* The Valiant Steed and Abyssal Steed AA abilities have been removed and the points refunded to all players who had these abilities.
* Existing Valiant Steed and Abyssal Steed items have been converted into Holy Steed and Unholy Steed items, respectively.

=== Zones & Population ===
* Fixed an issue where 3 NPCs in [[The Northern Desert of Ro|North Ro]] were flagged as named, despite the fact that they are obviously just Troopers.
* [[Malloy the Songbird]] in [[West Freeport|West Freepor]]<nowiki/>t no longer is tagged as a rare creature.
* [[Clockwork XIVB]] in [[Ak'Anon|Akanon]] should no longer show up as a humanoid.

=== Items ===
* [[Enchanted Fine Steel Morning Star]] is now usable by [[Beastlord|Beastlords]]
* Added a missing ornamentation socket to [[Ancient Spurned Waistcoat]].
* The various [[Soldier's Brooch Quest|Brooch]] rewards from the [[Rathe Mountains]] Froglok quest lines no longer have a level requirement.

=== Spells ===
* Improved spell stacking to prevent detrimental spells overwriting beneficial buffs when they impact, such as Hastes vs Slows, Movement Speed Buffs vs Snares, and Heal-Over-Time vs Damage-Over-Time spells. 
** In addition, detrimental spells will no longer strip beneficial spells from players when they contain the same effect type.
* Dispel spells are treated as detrimental for targeting in Spellblade procs.

=== Stances & Invocations ===
* The SpellBlade Invocation has been updated to work within a 2 second margin.
** e.g. If a spell's cast time is 4 seconds and it's re-use time is 6 seconds, this is a valid spell for SpellBlade.

=== UI ===
* Fixed an issue where some checkboxes and labels were word wrapping too soon when using fractional scaling.
* Right clicking on the spell gem in the actions window will now operate the same as right clicking else where in the list. Added an upgrade hint to the description section.
* Added a toggle to smooth out camera motion while in first person mode.
* Fixed an issue where an improper message would appear when trying to leave an instance in combat.

== 2026-08-25 - Patch Notes ==
These patch notes are from the Official EverQuest Legends discord, posted on August 25, 2026

=== [[The Estate of Unrest]] Revamp ===
* Added new items to most rare creatures within the zone.
* Improved some existing items within the zone.
* Undead monsters commonly seen on the first floor of the estate interior now occasionally drop Fine Steel weaponry.
* Rare monsters are now guaranteed to spawn with no placeholders.
* Several additional monsters recognizable as named are now flagged as rare creatures, and will benefit from increased mote drop rates.

=== [[Solusek's Eye]] ===
* Rare creatures in [[Solusek's Eye]] are now guaranteed spawns with no placeholders.
* Several additional monsters recognizable as named are now flagged as rare creatures, and will benefit from increased [[Mote Guide|mote drop]] rates.

=== Gameplay ===
* Decreased the amount of hitpoints that raid bosses have in multiplayer play within raid ([[voidling]]) zones.
* Fixed an issue where receiving an instance charge reset the timer to 1 hour when it should have been a remainder.
* Pets will no longer have their own faction and will no longer have their own aggro range.

=== Zones & Population ===
* Killing [[Pickclaw Goblins]] will now raise faction with [[Priests of Mischief]].
* NPC pets should no longer be capable of summoning a pet.

=== Quests ===
* Experience, faction, coin, items, and stats are now bulk calculated.
** Bulk quest item and coin turn-ins now pre-calculate results and display clearly in chat (max 4 'chat' blocks).
** Bulk quest turn-ins prevent FPS drops and resolve instantly.
** Coin quest NPCs now accept bulk quest turn-ins and will refund overage in the highest denomination.
* Quest NPCs will now accept coin in any denomination.
* Receiving multiple item rewards will display how many rewards you received.

=== Items ===
* Increased the runspeed of the [[Bristly Boar Reins]] by one speed tier.
* Players who have acquired the [[Torrid Corruptor]] can now retroactively grant themselves the quest title by right-clicking the item while it is equipped. Title may require zoning before it propagates.
* Increased the AC value of armor drops from [[Warlord Skarlon]].
* Added endurance to the [[Verishe Mal Greataxe]].
* Corrected tint on the Dark Mail items from [[Najena]].

===  AAs ===
* Fixed an issue where Full Potential would not be granted in some cases. 
** Affected players can swap loadouts once to receive this AA if they are missing the AA and their highest loadout is level 50.
* Added a new [[Beastlord]] AA Ability: Strike As One.
** This passive AA can be trained at level 35 or above for a cost of 6 AA points.
* Once trained, the [[Beastlord]] will have a chance on hit to proc the Strike As One buff, granted their Warder a 30% increased flurry chance for 12 seconds.

=== Spells ===
* Pets can now gain benefits from pet proc spell upgrades (damage, resists).
* Fixed an issue where summoning a familiar was interfering with pets properly re-leveling to their upgraded state after zoning.
* Fixed F1 (Target myself) targeting to always select the pet if both a pet and familiar are present.
* Added preview of updated spell effects when motes are added to the merge slot in the spell display window.
* Fixed a bug that can cause erratic spell cooldowns for instant-cast spells.

=== UI ===
* Fixed a bug where the instance menu could become unresponsive when editing keybinds.
* Right clicking on the spell gem in the actions window will now operate the same as right clicking else where in the list. Added an upgrade hint to the description section.
* Added the next charge time to the instance menu.
* Prevented tooltips from going off-screen while using window scaling.
* Fixed map centering when using scaling options.
* Fixed UI window scaling issues in modern UI where "keep on screen" settings were not being properly applied on full UI reload.
* Fixed UI reloading when not using "keep my settings."
* Fixed quantity drawing on the [[tradeskill]] window.
* Increased the maximum draw range of nameplate scaling in Options.
* Removed nameplate fonts from UI scaling to maintain readability.
* Resolved an issue with fonts that was contributing to issues with line breaks occurring too soon.
* Added modern input fields to the Social Hotkeys edit window (cut, copy, paste, cursor movement without shift, etc).
* Added 2 new nameplate options for aggro indicators:
** Mode 1 - Aggro mode. Nameplates will now have an outline and pulse their outline shadow in if the NPC has you targeted. This also applies a red, pulsing 'lasso' on the Extended Target window.
** Mode 2 - No-aggro mode. Applies the same styles, but only when the NPC is targeting a member of your group, or a group member's pet.

== 2026-08-18 - Patch Notes ==
These patch notes are from the Official EverQuest Legends discord, posted on August 18, 2026

=== Mistmoore Castle Revamped === 
* [[Mistmoore Castle]] has received a major upgrade!
* In addition to named NPCs being guaranteed spawns, they now all have a guaranteed loot drop of a common or rare item with stat bonuses. While some of these items are familiar to explorers of the castle in years past, many are brand new. Some include exciting new effects ready for you to enjoy as they are or turn into exaltations.
* All named enemies in the zone have now also been designated as rare creatures, vastly increasing their chances of dropping motes of potential.
* Additionally, the residents of the main castle are now somewhat less aggressive and will not react to your presence from extreme ranges... during the daytime. Exploring the castle at night, however, will still be a harrowing affair once the castle denizens have shown their true forms.

=== Fractional UI Scaling & Cursor Scaling === 
* The UI Scaling system now supports fractional ui scaling in .25 increments, ranging from 0.75x to 4.00x.
* The Cursor now has its own scaling factor in the in-game Options (O).
* A toggle now exists in the in-game Options (O) to use the Operating System cursor, rather than the in-game cursor.

=== Group Experience Bonus === 
* Grouping will now give a small experience bonus as intended.

=== Gameplay === 
* Increased the melee combat potential of [[Beastlord]] Warders substantially.
* Fixed an issue where raid invites would fail in certain circumstances.
* Non attackable NPCs can no longer multiclass.
* Address an issue where NPC corpses could continue walking even after they have died.
* Restored the original, Classic two-handed blunt animations to the game.
* You will no longer gain skillups from skills you haven't used when riposting.
* Creatures in the [[Plane of Fear]] and beyond should no longer fear or charm you so hard that you're unable to approach the game again for 24 hours.
* Fix for players getting charmed, and then shrunk by the pet scaling option ingame.
* Addressed an issue where NPCs would continue attacking each other after charm fades.
* Fixed a bug where [[Skill Cleave|cleave]] wasn't working with 1HB weapons.
* Updated the messages that appear while being stunned to clarify that you are now immune and that you are currently immune on subsequent hits.
* Fix an issue where zone specific music tracks would skip over music tracks if environmental sounds were disabled.
* Fix an issue where music would need to completely come to a stop before being able to resume the same track. The same track will now be able to resume the same sequence without having to fully have the track come to a stop.

=== Spells & AAs === 
* Targeted area effect lull spells, such as [[Harmony]], can now take effect on NPCs you have not engaged in combat.
* Mounts that are obtained from AAs will now only grant the Mount speed when you are a valid class for using that AA.
* Fixed an issue where a long (5-10 sec) recovery cooldown would fire if you used the Stop Action keybind with a Bard as one of your classes.
* Fixed an issue where range checks on contact [[Proc|procs]] like [[Vampiric Embrace]] would not work properly on NPCs with large hit boxes.
* The [[Lifespike]] spell has been moved from level 8 to level 5 for [[Shadow Knight|Shadowknights]].
* A new lifetap spell, [[Lifebite]], has been added at level 10 for [[Shadow Knight|Shadowknights]], and level 8 for [[Necromancer|Necromancers]]. 
** This new spell has been added to the autogrant list for both classes, and to the appropriate spell vendors.

=== Zones & Population === 
* The Wasps/Bees of [[Plane of Sky]] have seen had their stingers filed down while charmed.
* The Wasp/Bee in Plane of Sky known as 'Murderbee' should be a bit easier to exterminate in solo instances.
* Shimmering Meteors have also had their damage tuned downwards while charmed.
* Snow no longer overwrites the zone's precipitation type, preventing rain from falling. Praise Karana.
* Rain is no longer too small to see.
* Many wild animals should now be friendly towards [[Kerran]], similar to how they react to [[Ranger|Rangers]] & [[Druid|Druids]].
* Monsters should no longer try to patrol through walls in [[Runnyeye]].
* [[Seplawishinl Bladeblight]] in the [[Ocean of Tears]] now has a considerably shorter respawn timer.
* Fixed an issue where high level named monsters in [[Kedge Keep]] were taking an excessively long time to respawn.
* Non-raid boss NPCs are now restricted from casting charm if they already have a pet.

=== Quests === 
* The [[Soldier's Brooch Quest|Soldier's Brooch quest]] in [[Rathe Mountains]] will now allow the player to choose their reward.
* Updated the [[Torrid Corruptor]] final turn in to properly grant the quest completion title to some players that do not meet the 'lore' requirements of the quest.
* Players are now given the corresponding [[Potential of the Void]] task when they enter a raid instance.
* Upon entering a raid instance, all other [[Potential of the Void]] tasks are removed from the task list.

=== Items === 
* Corrected an issue that allowed Player Illusions to be used as Pet Illusions.
* As a result of this change, we have added a Conversion button to [[Guise of the Deceiver]] and [[Amulet of Necropotence]] that allows these items to be turned into a Pet Illusion version.
* [[Bloodmoon]] now has the Focus Effect [[Improved Vampirism III]].
* Fixed an issue preventing Armor [[Ornamentation Token|Ornamentation Tokens]] from working created from Cloth armor.
* [[Copper Band]] now has +1 AC.
* The Unholy Steed, Holy Steed, Abyssal Steed, and Valiant Steed AAs will now summon bridles, which can be used to summon the mount, instead of directly summoning the mount.
* Fix an issue where various item animations (such as whips and bows) were not animating on attack.
* Player pets are now prevented from equipping secondary-only items when they utilize a two-hander in their primary hand.

=== UI === 
* The search feature for spell inside the actions window has had its data expanded to be able to search many more fields.
* Added UI Scaling to the server selection screen.
* Fix an observed issue with spacing and scaling.
* Fix an observed issue where windows would not keep relative position and not keep on screen when resizing or rescaling.
* Adjusted inventory AC and weight labels to not include erroneous spacing.
* Scaling now applies before character select so that loading screen also scales properly.
* Fixed a Layout calculation bug that was causing the Actions window to produce graphical artifacts when shrinking the window vertically.
* On fresh installations of EverQuest Legends, a value for UI Scaling is now automatically detected and used.
* Changed UI Font Scaling to use dynamic re-rasterization.
* The map window should now be more compatible with UI Scaling.
* All context menus will now be fully kept on screen. This includes the spell list when you right click an empty gem.
* The Personal Instance window now properly shows respawning/non-respawning selections correctly.
* Fixed a display issue with the item inspection window that occurs after viewing an item that is convertible, such as the [[Gnoll Slayer]] item.
* A batch of new maps have arrived for the Maps window.
* Fixed a bug causing the Control Option 'momentary duck toggle' to not load its saved state.
* Added a new Options toggle in Interface->general to use the Actions/Spells window instead of the spellbook for the "Open Spellbook" keybind, and the Book Button on your spell bar.
* Added a button in the Spellbook to open the actions window to the Spells tab.
* Added that same toggle option from Options in the Spellbook for visibility.


