== 2026-07-14 - Pre-Order Beta Patch Notes ==
These patch notes are from the Official EverQuest Legends discord, posted on July 14, 2026
Patch notes are also available on the EverQuest Legends website [https://www.everquestlegends.com/patch-notes/eql-update-notes-7-14-2026 here]

=== General ===
* [[Crushbone]] has received a significant update!
** While the elves of Faydark were distracted with politics and intrigue, Clan Crushbone has been ceaselessly fortifying and multiplying it's army.
** The inhabitants of Faydark seek aid to quell the iron fist of [[Emperor Crush]] and the threat of open war.
** Let alone it's invaluable nostalgia, this early game dungeon features plenty of fresh loot and new enemies for adventurers to experience from levels 4 through 22.

* The [[Splitpaw Lair|Lair of the Splitpaw]] has received a significant update!
** Beginning with enemies from levels 25-28 at the entrance, the dungeon ramps through five difficulty bands. 
** In the highest level areas of the zone, standard enemies are levels 40-42. In each of these areas, named enemies can somewhat exceed the levels of the standard population.
** New rare spawns have been added, along with new and improved equipment drops. Rare spawn rates and equipment drop rates have also been substantially increased. 
** Expect to see guaranteed rare spawns in the lowest level areas of the dungeons, decreasing gradually until the highest level areas. 
** Named enemies will still appear very frequently even at the end of the dungeon!

=== AAs ===
* Quick buffing will now turn off any invocation then restore it after the quick buff finishes.

=== Gameplay ===
* Fixed an issue preventing weapon procs from triggering.
* NPCs with secondary melee classes will now be able to use those class combat skills like [[bash]], [[kick]], [[Skill Cleave|cleave]], [[frenzy]], [[backstab]], and monk kicks.
* Fixed an issue where your target was not cached when you start a cast, causing spells to land on the current target.
* [[Overseer Rael]] should now properly spawn in The Arena
* [[Chesgard Sydwen]] should no longer direct you to himself when asking him about the [[Bloodsabers]].
* [[The Estate of Unrest]] has seen fit to keep some its doors locked, meaning that adventurers should plan to go find the keys they need to navigate the estate.
* [[Tranixx Darkpaw]] will no longer terrorize the zonelines of [[Blackburrow]].
* [[Zok Zribb]], in the [[Froglok]] encampment in the [[Rathe Mountains]], has a new quest.
* [[Master Yael]] should no longer flee at low health.
* Added ladder to open grave, and gates across the false exit in [[Tutorial Zone|Tutorial]].
* [[The Muglwump]] will now actually spawn in a reasonable amount of time from instance creation.
* [[Mignar Mi' Draskch]] in [[Neriak]] Commons now sells the [[Wizard#Spells|Wizard Spells]] master list.
* [[Puntar Sandfisher|Puntar Sandfisher's]] corpse should no longer stand up and start creating pets. The body should also no longer be considerable.
* In Instance [[Voidlings]] can now See Invisible players.
* [[Lewis Reldnok|Lewis Reldnok's]] message for new [[Gnome|Gnomish]] [[Paladin|Paladins]] should be less confusing now.
* The [[voidlings]] that create raid instances should no longer appear inside of [[Personal Instance|personal instances]].
* Fixed a bug causing group EXP to not be calculated correctly in some scenarios
* Implemented changes to raid targets to better scale with group size<br />

===  Items ===
* All [[Item Upgrade System#Motes of Potential Experience Rules|Motes of Potential]] are no longer tradable.
* Drakkin no longer appears as an option when using a [[User:Alanna/Alanna's Race Unlock Guide|Race Unlock Token]].

===  Skills & Disciplines ===
* Added [[Disrupting Shot]], a new Discipline/Combat Ability for [[Ranger|Rangers]].
** Available at level 20.
** Does a small amount of damage, and interrupts the targets casting.
* Added [[Tendon Slice]], a new Discipline/Combat Ability for [[Berserker|Berserkers]].
** Available at level 14.
** Snares your opponent, lowering their movement speed.
* Added [[Skull Bash]], a new Discipline/Combat Ability for [[Berserker|Berserkers]].
** Available at level 20.
** Stuns your opponent.
* Players should no longer forage up out of era items in the [[Tutorial Zone|Tutorial]], or the [[New Sebilisian Expedition]].

===  Spells & Spell Upgrading ===
* Fix tier 1 upgraded summon item spells so they properly create +1 items.
* The [[Spell Upgrading|spell upgrade]] boost to summoned item tiers now applies to items summoned within a container, such as Summon: Phantom Plate.
* [[Spell Upgrading|Spell upgrades]] now boost damage to bard AoE songs, such as [[Denon's Disruptive Discord]].
* Upgraded pets will now remain upgraded across zonelines.
* Upgraded pets will now cast spells at their upgraded level.
* [[Spell Upgrading|Spell upgrades]] will now increase the level cap efficiency for pacify, fear, & stun spells.
* The [[Ranger]] spells [[Firefist]], [[Nature's Precision]], and [[Force of Nature]] will no longer try to overwrite the lower level spells in the book as you attempt to scribe them.

===  Stances & Invocations ===
* Fixed an issue impacting resist interactions with OverChannel [[Stances & Invocations#Invocations|Invocation]].
* Re-enabled OverChannel resistance bonuses for buff-based resistance checks
* Empower now applies to bard AoE songs, such as [[Denon's Disruptive Discord]].
* The divine invocation will now target self pets and group pets (at 20% and 40% lower HP priority, respectively)

===  UI ===
* Updated Actions Window macros (socials) tab to a scrollable list instead of paged buttons.
** The Actions window macros tab is now a scrollable list with searchable and sortable entries.
** Right click on any row to open the editor.
** Left click on the button activates the macro while right click either cancels an active macro or if not busy opens the editor.
** Macro keys on the hotbuttons bar now colorize their text per their macro editor assignment and show as depressed as long as an activated macro is running with /pause delays.
** The use of a /timer with a macro still creates the cooldown overlay.
* [[Stances & Invocations|Stance/Invocation]] bar hidden context menu should now sync properly allowing you to unhide stances and invocations.
* Fix [[Item Upgrade System|merging]] to equipment items and allow merging to activated items inventory (including from loot window).
* [[Spell Upgrading|Spell upgrades]]: Motes to-be-consumed will now appear with a red border in the inventory (similar to item merging).
* Ethernere Tainted Karana will no longer show up in the find window in the [[Western Plains of Karana]].
* Renamed the "Augmentation" Tab to "[[Exaltations|Exaltation]]" on the Storage tab for default / default_light / default_modern.

== 2026-07-07 - Pre-Order Beta Patch Notes ==
These patch notes are from the Official EverQuest Legends discord, posted on July 7, 2026

Patch notes are also available on the EverQuest Legends website [https://www.everquestlegends.com/patch-notes/eql-update-notes-7-7-2026 here]

=== Instances === 
All instances should now work properly! 

Today's patch addressed several issues preventing instances from spinning up ingame and displaying errors on attempting to enter. These include, but are not limited to:
* Removed errant charge check for DZ invites to multiplayer raid instance.
* When you leave a personal instance you will now be placed at zone safe coords.
* Leaving an instance will now put you in the base zone. ([[Difficulty Level#Difficulty 0: The Beginner's Comfort Zone|Difficulty 0]])
* A personal instance charge is now only consumed upon successful entry to the zone.
* Fixed replay timers occurring on adding a group member to a [[Personal Instance|personal instance zone]].
* Players can now enter instances of the zone they are in, regardless of [[Difficulty Level|difficulty]] or pickzone.

=== General===
'''Spell Tiering Phase 2'''
* Pet Upgrades
** Summon Pet / Warder spells will now add the rank of the spell to the summoned pet's level, capped at player level -1.
** Each upgraded pet level will increase hp by 6%, add 1 base damage, and add 5 skill points.
** Enabled pet inventory for charmed NPC pets.
** Charmed pets now equip from the pet inventory slots and those items are removed when charm breaks.
** Charmed pets now report their inventory of player given equipped items.

* Spell Upgrades
** Spell upgrades now have damage and healing bonuses.
** Spellblade, Quickbuff and Symphonic Aura now trigger upgraded spells/songs.
** Spell upgrade duration effects now work for lull effects.
** Added rounding to spell upgrade duration calculations to help scaling of small values. (2 or 3 ticks)
** Max level of crowd control effects (mez, charm) increased by spell tier.
** 10% chance per spell tier to not consume reagents for spells that require reagents. Reagent costs are skipped at tier 10.
** Summon item spells will now summon item's tier to the spell tier if the item is upgradable.
*** e.g. - Summoned Dagger X will now summon a Summoned: Dagger +10
** Combat Innate Buffs with procs are cast at one half of the buff's spell tier level.
*** e.g. [[Vampiric Embrace]] X (Buff) will cast Vampiric Embrace V (Proc)
=== Alternate Advancement (AAs) === 
* Added the following [[Alternate Advancement#Class AAs|Class AAs]].  Note that the AAs themselves have no effect, just give visibility and explanation to pre-existing passive bonuses to the listed class.
** Innate Divine Healing - Cleric
** Innate Fighters Tenacity - Warrior
** Innate Called Shot - Ranger
** Innate Power Strike - Berserker
** Innate Sneakiness - Rogue
=== Gameplay === 
* Locked doors in [[Najena]] will now search bags for keys instead of requiring the key to be held on the cursor.
* [[Drelzna]] will no longer rapidly proc [[Harm Touch]].
* Zombies in [[Misty Thicket]] should now appear slightly more zombie-like.
* Tradeskill vendors in the [[New Sebilisian Expedition]] are now on the proper faction.
* While in [[Plane of Sky]] you can now summon normal non-scaled pets.
* Doing quests for [[Da Bashers|Da Bashers of Grobb]] will now also increase your standing with the [[Grobb Merchants]].
* Buff effects on players and pets with upgraded levels now persist across camping and zoning.

=== Items === 
* Removed low level item haste cap. Standard haste cap rules still apply.
* The various Wind Runes from the [[Plane of Sky]] can now be held in [[Currency Storage]].
* The [[Golden Crescent Key]] used in the [[Najena]] dungeon is no longer Temporary/NO RENT

=== Skills & Disciplines === 
* Improved [[taunt]] success rates, most no`[[Skill Cleave|Cleave]] and [[Bash]] are no longer on shared timers.
* [[Blood Draw Venom]] should now correctly do more damage than Blood Siphon Venom.
* [[Paralytic Poison]] now correctly triggers the Weakening Strike, instead of Hobbling Strike.

=== Spells === 
*The following spells can now only be casted on group members, your pet, or your self.
** [[Scale of Wolf]]
** [[Boon of the Garou]]
** [[Spirit of the Puma]]
** [[Impassivity]]
** [[Stoicism]]
** [[Nonchalance]]
** [[Snails Healing]]
** [[Tortoises Healing|Tortoises healing]]
** [[Slugs Healing|Slugs healing]]
* [[Stoicism]] and [[Slugs Healing]] have both had their heal per tick increased from 160 to 200.
* The final heal of the [[Druid|Druid's]] "[[Blooming Heal|Bloom]]" spells is now affected by AAs.
* [[Druid]] "[[Blooming Heal|Bloom]]" heals now have a more appropriate visual effect when they Bloom.
* [[Blooming Heal]] description now accurately reports that its Bloom heals for 300, not 200.
* Rain spells will no longer hit npc's not on the aggro list.
* [[Beastlord]] Warders will now have mana, allowing them to actually cast their spells.
* Significantly increased the melee capabilities of [[Beastlord]] Warders.

=== Stances & Invocations === 
* Regeneration modifiers from [[Stances & Invocations|stances and invocations]] always apply even if they are not active while out of combat as long as you have access to the stance/invocation.
* Empowering and Overchannel invocations now work on damage over time and heal over time spells.
* Empowering effects and costs were reduced to balance out spell upgrade bonuses.
* Reverted Arcane Mastery to prior values.

=== UI === 
* Display summoned pet stats on inventory window pet tab.
** Summoned pets will show their HP, Mana, AC, Regens, and other stats on pet inventory tab.
** Pets will now benefit from for the following equipped item bonuses: Attack, HP Regen,  Mana Regen
** Pets should now better show the impact of buffs to: HP, Mana
** Improved HP management when adding/removing items from pets.
** Improved HP adjustments when entering/exiting charm.
* Improved Colors of Login Server Text
* Fixed a missing flag preventing heal crits from showing up in logs.
* Fixed an issue where client showed incorrect max level for some toggleable AAs.
* [[Difficulty Level|Difficulty]] button menu will now function properly after right clicking on the difficulty button.
* Opacity and spell filtering now work for spell particles.
* Added a toggle to filter beneficial [[Bard#Songs|bard songs]] to make symphonic auras less bulky.
* Fixed clients display of alternate ability caps.
* [[Stances & Invocations|Stance/Invocation]] bar visibility should now save properly.
* Fixed which default INI file the UI should use based on resolution of the game window.
* The message for shielding now goes to the skills filter.
* Options window context menu's will now function properly such as alpha.
* [[Stances & Invocations|Stance/Invocation]] ability hot buttons and buttons in actions window now use matching icons from stance bar.
* Actions Window stances/invocation highlight boxes will no longer be rendered when not on abilities tab. Gate ritual now shows your bind location rather than your origin.
* Buff effects now indicate the upgrade level of the cast spell (spell names, tooltips, display info window).
* Updated various displayed spell names in ui and chat to use the upgraded spell name (appends suffix).
* Spell display window now shows resistance debuff benefits for detrimental spells.
* Added the upgraded spell title to the 'begin casting' chat messages.
* Fixed intermittent "must select target to cast spell" for item [[Clickies|clicky]] effects & [[rituals]].

== 2026-07-03 - Hotfix ==
